DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI AutomationBuilderPage shipped at parity with the web source: an
@Observable AutomationBuilderPageModel (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injected
AutomationBuilderDataSource whose 7 method names mirror the ported web hooks verbatim (useAutomation /
useAutomationPreset / useVehicles / useNotificationChannels / useCreateAutomationFull /
useUpdateAutomationFull / useTestRunAutomation). The page reproduces the web PageContainer chrome
(create/edit/preset title + subtitle + breadcrumb + Back), all four page data states (loading skeleton /
retryable error / "not found" empty / the form), and the typed builder form: General (name /
description / vehicle / enabled), When (trigger-type picker + the GlassPanel1 configurator /
GlassPanel2 empty), Only If (conditions), Then (actions), conflict warnings, the save-error banner,
the Save / Test Run / Cancel bar, the unsaved-changes discard dialog, and the GlassPanel3 preset hint —
built on P2 tokens + P3 shared components (TSGlassPanel / TSFormSection / TSTextField / TSToggle /
TSButton / TSEmptyState / TSErrorDisplay / TSSkeleton / TSAlertBanner / motion), composing the real
sibling editor surfaces (no duplicated logic); adaptive macOS/iPad vs iPhone-compact; every visible
string from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names; VoiceOver labels/traits + Dynamic Type + SI
(no non-SI stored/computed). Verified by real iOS-18 + macOS-15 Swift 6 strict-concurrency
swiftc -typecheck (0/0), an executed 32/32 model harness, and a GREEN full-app xcodebuild
(Release/-Onone/arm64). The default-Debug xcodebuild + xcodebuild test are RED ONLY for the
pre-existing, out-of-scope toolchain-drift reasons enumerated above (preview Sema / missing x86_64
slice / SIL-optimizer crash / unrelated broken *Tests.swift) — the identical disposition under which
the sibling p4-apple/P7/page:automations/AutomationsList was accepted DONE.

